---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "../components/ui/Container.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to print your chess book — Me Chess Book"
  description="The few print-dialog settings that make a clean chess book PDF: exact page size, no margins, background graphics on, headers and footers off."
  path="/how-to-print"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Printing", path: "/how-to-print" }]}
>
  <section
    class="on-ink grid-ink border-b border-line-ink bg-ink pt-[clamp(6rem,12vw,8rem)] pb-[clamp(2.5rem,5vw,3.5rem)]"
  >
    <Container>
      <p class="comment">
        <span class="slash" aria-hidden="true">//</span> the printed page
      </p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 max-w-[24ch] font-display text-[clamp(2.2rem,5.4vw,3.6rem)] leading-[1.02] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance text-cream"
      >
        How to print your book
      </h1>
      <p
        class="mt-5 max-w-[44rem] text-[clamp(1rem,1.4vw,1.1rem)] leading-[1.6] text-[rgba(250,250,244,0.72)]"
      >
        The book is laid out at the exact size of the paper, so once the print
        dialog matches that size there is nothing to adjust. Five settings are
        all that matter.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </section>

  <section class="grid-paper border-b border-line py-12 sm:py-16">
    <Container>
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_20rem]">
        <div class="max-w-[46rem]">
          <h2
            class="font-display text-[1.6rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em]"
          >
            1. Make the book first
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink-soft">
            On the <a class="underline decoration-yellow decoration-2 underline-offset-2" href="/make">Make a book</a> page, enter your username and choose your settings. Note the page size you picked — you will select the same one in the print dialog.
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-10 font-display text-[1.6rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em]"
          >
            2. Open the print dialog
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink-soft">
            Press the <strong>Print</strong> button, or use <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>P</kbd> (<kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>P</kbd> on a Mac). Chrome or Edge are recommended: they handle exact page sizes and background graphics most reliably.
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-10 font-display text-[1.6rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em]"
          >
            3. Set five options
          </h2>
          <ol class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-ink-soft">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="font-mono font-bold text-yellow-deep">01</span>
              <span><strong>Paper size</strong> — the size you chose (A4 or A5).</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="font-mono font-bold text-yellow-deep">02</span>
              <span><strong>Margins</strong> — set to <em>None</em>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="font-mono font-bold text-yellow-deep">03</span>
              <span><strong>Scale</strong> — leave at <em>100%</em> (or <em>Default</em>); do not use &ldquo;Fit to page&rdquo;.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="font-mono font-bold text-yellow-deep">04</span>
              <span><strong>Background graphics</strong> — <em>on</em>. This prints the cover art and the dark chessboard squares.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="font-mono font-bold text-yellow-deep">05</span>
              <span><strong>Headers and footers</strong> — <em>off</em>, so no date or URL is added.</span>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <h2
            class="mt-10 font-display text-[1.6rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em]"
          >
            4. Save as a PDF
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink-soft">
            Choose <em>Save as PDF</em> as the destination to get a file you can keep or send to a printer, or pick your printer to print it directly. If you are printing a physical copy, print <strong>double-sided</strong> (flip on the long edge); the book is padded to an even number of pages so the sheets line up.
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-10 font-display text-[1.6rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.01em]"
          >
            5. To have it bound
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-[1.7] text-ink-soft">
            For a proper book, send the PDF to a bindery such as <a class="underline decoration-yellow decoration-2 underline-offset-2" href="https://mixam.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mixam</a>. A5 is a good pocket size; A4 is easier to read. The PDF is already the right size and needs no bleed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="no-print">
          <div class="panel">
            <h2 class="panel__title">Print cheat-sheet</h2>
            <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-3 font-mono text-[0.8rem]">
              <li class="flex justify-between gap-4 border-b border-line pb-2">
                <span class="text-muted">Paper size</span><span>A4 / A5</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex justify-between gap-4 border-b border-line pb-2">
                <span class="text-muted">Margins</span><span>None</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex justify-between gap-4 border-b border-line pb-2">
                <span class="text-muted">Scale</span><span>100%</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex justify-between gap-4 border-b border-line pb-2">
                <span class="text-muted">Background graphics</span><span>On</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex justify-between gap-4">
                <span class="text-muted">Headers &amp; footers</span><span>Off</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="panel mt-6">
            <h2 class="panel__title">If something looks wrong</h2>
            <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-4 text-[0.9rem] leading-[1.6]">
              <div>
                <dt class="font-bold">Board squares are blank</dt>
                <dd class="text-ink-soft">
                  Background graphics is off. Turn it on and print again.
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="font-bold">Pages have a border of white</dt>
                <dd class="text-ink-soft">
                  Margins are not set to <em>None</em>, or the scale is not 100%.
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="font-bold">Extra blank sheets</dt>
                <dd class="text-ink-soft">
                  Headers and footers are on; they add a margin line to every page.
                </dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
